{# oss-readiness-auditor: rule source #}
<section class="s" id="method"><h2>Method and rules</h2><p class="intro">The complete rule set of this run. A rule finds candidates; whether a candidate is a real problem is for the reviewer to decide – that is why many checks end in “needs judgement”. Files scanned: those tracked by git (or all files outside build folders if there is no git).</p>
<div class="rules">
{% for c in checks %}
<details id="m-{{ c.id }}"><summary>{{ icon(c.icon) }}{{ c.title }}</summary><dl>
{% for r in c.rules %}<dt>{{ r.name }}</dt><dd>{{ r.detail }}</dd>
{% endfor %}
</dl></details>
{% endfor %}
</div></section>
